"""A weak orthographic/boundary approximation, not a semantic detector.

Most tokens receive a value close to zero. The larger rules concern document
openings: common words tend positive, spelled-out numbers negative, and a few
formatting characters have strong offsets. Elsewhere UTF-8 continuation pieces
are negative, with small script and punctuation adjustments. Fine token-specific
variation is deliberately left unexplained. Two strong opening-prefix responses,
"12" and "Title:", are retained explicitly.
