"""Approximate a short-word-piece L detector, strongest for Arabic lam.

Lam inside a word is much stronger than lam in a spaced Arabic article.
Its neighbouring letters and a short suffix echo refine that estimate.
Short Latin L syllables get larger values in Turkish-like text, identified
causally from completed words' Turkish versus English frequencies.
A separate document-initial `Title:` cue accounts for a large metadata spike.
This is a spelling approximation; many less systematic L responses are missed.
